\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Decoder block}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{transformer}

\p{A \newvocab{decoder block} is a shape-preserving map on hidden-state
sequences formed from a causally masked self-attention sublayer and a
pointwise feed-forward sublayer. Each sublayer has a residual connection and
a declared normalization placement.}

\p{The two-sublayer decoder construction appears in
\citet{sec. 3.1}{vaswani2017attention}. The original encoder-decoder model also
has cross-attention in its decoder. A decoder-only language model omits that
cross-attention sublayer, as described in
\citet{sec. 6, Decoder-only transformers}{phuong2022formal}.}
